N0JCG client-side Packet RMS Pat build

Base: official Pat v0.17.0 and wl2k-go v0.12.1.

In connect.go, keep outgoing Packet RMS sessions in the normal FBB client-turn
mode (`exchange(conn, url.Target, false)`) so the client sends `FF` after the
handshake. The client-specific behavior is implemented in wl2k-go/fbb: it
accepts the RMS prompt/challenge and sends the standard client handshake.

In wl2k-go/fbb/handshake.go, preserve server-side behavior but, for the
client-initiated exchange, consume the RMS SID/challenge/prompt and always
send the complete standard FBB client handshake after the prompt. The
handshake includes `;FW`, the Pat SID, and `;PR` when challenged. Returning
without sending the handshake leaves BPQ in terminal mode and produces an
idle session with only RR acknowledgements.

The resulting ARM64 binary is `tools/pat-winlink-client-rms`. Telnet and
non-AX.25 transports retain Pat's original server-led handshake behavior.
